        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-15T17:03:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh now that is a good question. Almost certainly not.\nLooking at our existing clients, one just ignores failure (but the host will kill the VM after a timeout if it doesn\u0027t get the notification), and two call abort.\n\nWhat would you suggest? Document that, or make this return void and abort() itself on failure?",
      "parentUuid": "026e3872_102c2746",
      "revId": "55da89c9ca0d6e59d40d1fc87f4383723edc087a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fc03d1f_e9bbf7ac",
        "filename": "microdroid/vm_payload/include/vm_payload.h",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 36,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006497
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-17T16:34:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the client really can\u0027t do anything, I\u0027d probably make this a `void` function and then implement whatever strategy makes sense internally.\n\nPlease consider the same question for any of the functions returning `bool` below as well, and if clients can do something about the failure, whether you should return an error code instead of a boolean to give more context on the failure type.",
      "parentUuid": "59252eec_6b95fc3b",
      "revId": "55da89c9ca0d6e59d40d1fc87f4383723edc087a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2bf6e8cc_0fac5c40",
