        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-25T10:58:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, that was definitely food for thought. It goes against the grain a bit, but after some reflection I think you\u0027re right.\n\nFor most of the functions there isn\u0027t anything useful the client can do and so I\u0027ve changed them to abort on failure and return void - see aosp/2314859.\n\nAnd then I looked again at AVmPayload_runVsockRpcServer. That is even odder - if it fails then again really the client can\u0027t do anything about it. But if it succeeds, it actually never returns - which is the normal behavior.\n\nSo I documented that oddness and also made it panic on failure, over in aosp/2317213. That has the latest version of vm_payload.h in it.\n\n(Since I moved the files around and rebased things the diff here is a bit confusing; sorry about that.)",
      "parentUuid": "7fc03d1f_e9bbf7ac",
